From 89fef09581fcccc12f351988519b328bb2f13cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:22:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 63/71] Assemble a streamed assistant message into one content
 part

A Chat stream delivers an assistant message a token at a time, and the SSE
reader pushed one `ContentItem::OutputText` per delta, so a finished message
carried 25-54 parts. That is invisible while the parts are concatenated - the
request builder does `text.push_str(t)` - but `content_items_to_text` rejoins
them with a newline, which is right for the Responses API, where a completed
message arrives whole from `response.output_item.done`. On this wire it put a
newline between every single token.

The retired verbatim assistant tail was the one hot caller: measured over the
332 assistant messages retained by the recorded compactions, 45,101 tokens as
stored against 21,773 for the same text concatenated - 2.07x, paid for on every
request that carried the tail, and mangled prose for the model to read. The
remaining callers are a fallback in the memories runtime that only fires when no
text delta arrived, plus the guardian and realtime paths, neither of which runs
against this provider.

Both halves are upstream's and correct apart from each other, so the fix belongs
at the source, in this fork's wire adapter: coalesce into the last part and hand
the rest of the code the single part it expects. Verified on a live session -
one content part, 1.00x against the concatenated text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/codex-api/src/sse/chat.rs | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/codex-api/src/sse/chat.rs b/codex-rs/codex-api/src/sse/chat.rs
index a2931b5585..eb72066624 100644
--- a/codex-rs/codex-api/src/sse/chat.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/codex-api/src/sse/chat.rs
@@ -409,7 +409,16 @@ async fn append_assistant(
     }
 
     if let Some(ResponseItem::Message { content, .. }) = assistant {
-        content.push(ContentItem::OutputText { text: text.clone() });
+        // Coalesce deltas into one part. A Chat stream delivers a message a token at a time, and
+        // one `OutputText` per delta leaves the finished item with hundreds of parts. Consumers
+        // that rejoin those parts with a separator - `content_items_to_text` joins with a newline,
+        // which is correct for the Responses API, where a completed message arrives whole - then
+        // put that separator between every token. Building the single part the rest of the code
+        // expects keeps the two wires equivalent.
+        match content.last_mut() {
+            Some(ContentItem::OutputText { text: existing }) => existing.push_str(&text),
+            _ => content.push(ContentItem::OutputText { text: text.clone() }),
+        }
         let _ = tx_event
             .send(Ok(ResponseEvent::OutputTextDelta(text)))
             .await;
